course: dictionary
lesson: 13742
title: Words that mix: interbred
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Interbred is the past form of interbreed. Inter means between, and breed means to have young. So interbred means two different kinds of animals or plants mated and had young together. Read the words around it to check.
explain: «Lions and tigers have interbred in zoos.» The clues are lions and tigers, which are different kinds, and the babies they have. So interbred means they bred together. Always ask: were the parents of the same kind, or different kinds?
explain: In science, interbred can also mean that genes mixed. «Long ago, early humans and Neanderthals interbred.» Swap in mixed: their genes mixed, which is why some people today carry a little Neanderthal DNA. The meaning still fits, so you have understood it.
fact: Interbred is the past form of interbreed: today they interbreed, yesterday they interbred.
fact: «Interbred» means bred together, so two different kinds of animals or plants mated and had young.
fact: In science, interbred means the young mixed genes from two different groups, species or varieties.
fact: A mule is the young of a horse and a donkey, so horses and donkeys have interbred.
fact: Phrases to know: interbred with, have interbred. Example: «Farmers have interbred plants to get new varieties.»
exercise: «Horses and donkeys have interbred to make mules.» What does interbred mean here? | *Bred together, so two different kinds had young | Were kept in separate fields | Fought in a race | Ran away from each other
exercise: Which word is the past form of interbreed? | interbreeding | interbreeds | *interbred
exercise: «Early humans and Neanderthals interbred long ago.» What does this suggest about their genes? | Stayed completely separate forever | Became the same as lions | *Mixed together, so some people today carry Neanderthal DNA | Disappeared at once
test: «Farmers have interbred plants to get new varieties.» Which meaning fits interbred best? | Sold at the market | *Bred together to make new kinds | Cut down | Grew in separate fields
test: Choose the right form: Yesterday, the two kinds of bird ___ in the wild. | interbreeds | *interbred | interbreed
exam: «Ligers are babies born after lions and tigers have interbred.» Why is interbred the right word here? | Because the lions were happy | Because the sentence is about fighting | *Because the parents were different kinds that mated and had young | Because the babies are small
